  { q: 'Are all ravens in the genus Corvus?', a: 'Yes. All species called "raven" belong to the genus Corvus (family Corvidae). However, the genus also includes crows, rooks, jackdaws, and choughs, so "Corvus" does not mean "raven". The boundary between "raven" and "crow" is partly a matter of common naming convention, not a strict phylogenetic division.' },
